- Metro Manufacturing has a strong cash position with $5.2M on the balance sheet and a conservative net burn of $72K/month. At current net burn, we have ~72 months of runway (5.2M / 72K ≈ 72.2 months). Revenue last quarter was $670K (≈ $223K/month), which helps fund operations and explains the low net burn.
Key drivers and trend
- Revenue contribution: Quarterly revenue of $670K (~$223K/month) materially offsets operating spend.
- Expense posture: Gross operating spend is roughly $295K/month (reconciles to revenue − net burn), indicating disciplined cost management.
- Burn trend: Net burn is low and stable, giving us flexibility for strategic investments (R&D, sales expansion) or opportunistic M&A without immediate financing needs.
Implications and recommendation
- With >5 years of runway, prioritize growth investments that have clear ROI: accelerate high-ROI sales/marketing, invest in product initiatives, or selectively hire in revenue-generating roles.
- Maintain scenario planning (12–36 month) and monitor leading indicators (bookings, AR days, large customer concentration).
