There’s an inconsistency: 72K/month net burn implies ~72 months runway, not 20 months. Typical explanations:
- “Burn” could be defined differently (gross burn vs net burn). Gross burn = total cash spending; net burn = gross burn minus revenue. If $72K is net burn, runway is ~72 months. If someone quoted 20 months, they probably used a different expense baseline (planned investments, one-time commitments, or used gross burn).
- Or the 20-month figure may include upcoming hires/capex that increase monthly burn to ~$260K.

Please confirm which definition is intended (net vs gross burn) or whether the 20-month runway includes planned investments. Meanwhile, below are materials you can use for internal presentation based on both interpretations.

