- Finance narrative (short):
  “At current net cash burn of ~$72K/month, our cash position provides substantial runway (~6 years). This reflects recurring revenue of ~$223K/month against operating spend that results in modest net cash usage. The extended runway gives us optionality to invest in targeted growth initiatives while maintaining conservative liquidity coverage. We recommend continued focus on margin improvement and monitoring of one‑time capital needs to preserve this runway.”
- Risks & action items (short bullets):
  - Monitor revenue seasonality; a sustained revenue decline would increase net burn.
  - Validate one-time capital or working capital needs that are not in run rate.
  - Consider using runway to accelerate high-ROI growth investments or to refinance only if strategic.

