  “Metro Manufacturing has $5.2M in cash and roughly 20 months of runway at current burn, implying cash usage of ~ $260K/month. Last quarter revenue was $670K (~$223K/month).”
- Finance narrative (short):
  “With an implied monthly cash outflow of ~ $260K, our current cash covers about 20 months of operations at today’s run rate. Revenue last quarter (~$223K/month) offsets some of our expenses, but the remaining gap requires active management of expense growth and continued revenue acceleration. Given this runway, we should target fundraising or meaningful margin improvement with a 9–12 month buffer before cash becomes constrained.”
- Risks & action items:
  - Build a 12-month cash forecast and initiate fundraising preparations if we want >12 months of dry powder.
  - Identify near-term cost reductions or revenue acceleration levers to extend runway (e.g., pricing, large customer pipeline, renegotiating supplier terms).
  - Stress test forecast for downside scenarios (e.g., 10–20% revenue shortfall).

3) Suggested charts and slides to include (what the audience will want)
