- Monthly net cash burn trend (last 6–12 months) vs last quarter revenue line — show whether net burn is increasing or decreasing.
- Runway sensitivity table: runway in months at range of net burn values (e.g., $50K, $100K, $150K, $260K).
- Key drivers waterfall: starting cash, revenue, opex, one-time items, capex, ending cash.
- Trigger timeline: when to start fundraising, target milestones, and cushion policy (e.g., target 12 months cash post raise).

