- Cash on hand = $5.2M
- Revenue last quarter = $670K → average monthly revenue ≈ $670K / 3 = $223K/month
- If burn = $72K/month → implied net cash flow = revenue (223K) − burn (72K) = +$151K/month (i.e., cash would be increasing; runway would not be a constraint)
- If runway = 20 months → implied net burn = 5.2M / 20 = $260K/month (net cash outflow)
