Drivers & trend
- Revenue growth over the quarter is the primary cash driver; core operating expenses are tightly controlled (payroll/SG&A ≈ $72K/month).
- Positive near-term cash flow provides runway to scale sales and R&D, while maintaining a conservative cash buffer.
Risks & actions
- Monitor accounts receivable days and one-time cash outflows (capex, deferred payments). If growth requires stepped-up investment, model the timing and size of hiring/capex.
- Action items: continue tight control of discretionary spend, allocate incremental cash to highest-return growth levers, and run a 3–12 month scenario to test hiring or capex moves.

