Summary
- Metro Manufacturing holds $5.2M in cash and generated $670K last quarter (~$223K/month). The company’s runway is 20 months, implying a current net cash burn of ~$260K/month.
Drivers & trend
- Net cash outflows significantly exceed operating revenue, indicating elevated spending (could be due to planned investment, high COGS, capex, or one-off costs).
- If this pace continues, cash declines steadily; the company must either increase revenue, reduce spend, or access capital within the next 18–20 months to maintain operations.
Risks & actions
- Immediate priorities: identify and quantify the components of the $260K/month net burn (operating vs. one-time items).
- Run scenarios (base, downside, upside) modeling revenue growth, cost cuts, and financing options.
- Action items: freeze non-essential hiring, prioritize high-ROI projects, accelerate receivable collections, and prepare a capital plan (bridge, raise, or strategic financing).

