- “As of [date], Metro Manufacturing holds $5.2M in cash and reported $670K revenue in Q[ ] (≈$223K/month). Depending on classification of current expenditures, net cash burn is either low (~$72K/month, giving positive operational cash flow) or materially higher (implied net burn ≈$260K/month if runway is 20 months). We are reconciling the difference now, but next steps are to (1) finalize monthly cash-flow detail, (2) produce a 12–24 month scenario analysis, and (3) identify immediate cost-savings and financing options if needed. A prioritization of projects and a near-term capital plan will be ready by [target date].”

