- Define burn: clarify whether burn is net (expenses – revenue) or gross (operating expenses) and whether runway includes planned one-time spends.
- If runway = 20 months, what specific one-time or recurring items create that burn? (hiring, capex, M&A diligence, strategic inventory buildup)
- What are the top 3 levers to extend runway by 6–12 months? (reduce discretionary spend, accelerate receivables, increase short-term sales incentives)
- What are go/no-go milestones for any planned investments (hire, new plant, tooling)?

Immediate next steps I can do for you
- Reconcile the numbers: I can model both scenarios (72 months vs 20 months) side-by-side with a table and sensitivity analysis — tell me which figure is authoritative or share last 12 months P&L/Cash flow and I’ll build the forecast.
