Quick math / data check
- Cash: $5,200,000
- Stated burn: $72,000/month
- Stated runway: 20 months
- Revenue (last quarter): $670,000 → monthly revenue ≈ $223,333

Inconsistency:
- If net burn = $72,000/month, runway = 5,200,000 / 72,000 ≈ 72.2 months (not 20 months).
- If runway = 20 months, implied net burn = 5,200,000 / 20 = $260,000/month (not $72K).
Please confirm whether the $72K is:
  - net cash burn (expenses minus revenue), or
  - gross cash burn (total cash outflows, before revenue), or
  - something else (e.g., operating burn excluding one-time items).

Numbers implied by each interpretation
- Scenario A — net burn = $72K/month
  - Runway ≈ 72.2 months (~6 years).
