Talking points / implications:
- Start fundraising discussions or strategic alternatives within the next 6–9 months (aim to close before runway approaches 6–9 months).
- Tighten discretionary spend, re-evaluate hires and capital projects, and model 3 downside scenarios (10%, 25%, 50% revenue declines and cost-reduction responses).
- Produce a rolling 12–24 month cash forecast with monthly granularity and trigger levels for actions.

Recommended slides / charts for internal materials
- Executive summary slide (1–2 bullets): cash, runway, last quarter revenue, one-sentence recommendation.
- Cash & runway calculation (show the formula and the number).
- Monthly cash flow forecast (12–24 months) with a baseline and 2–3 scenarios (best / base / downside).
- Burn trend chart (monthly net burn over last 12 months) — highlights direction and any one-offs.
- Revenue trend & composition (MRR/ARR if applicable, quarter-over-quarter growth).
- Key KPIs table: cash, runway, net burn, monthly revenue, gross margin %, CAC/LTV if tracked.
- Action plan slide with triggers (e.g., fundraise when runway = 9–12 months; cut discretionary spend if runway falls below 12 months).

Suggested metrics and checks to include
- Net burn (monthly): Opex + Capex - Revenue
- Gross burn (total cash outflows)
- Monthly recurring revenue (MRR) and churn (if applicable)
- Cash runway under scenarios (base, -10% revenue, +10% cost)
- Break-even month (if achievable by cost reductions or revenue improvement)

Example wording you can drop into a slide or email (pick the matching scenario)

If burn = $72K:
“As of [date], cash on hand is $5.2M and quarterly revenue was $670K (≈$2.68M annual run-rate). Net burn is currently ~$72K/month, providing ~72 months of runway. We recommend focusing on growth investments with disciplined monthly cash monitoring and maintaining a 12–18 month minimum cash cushion.”

If runway = 20 months:
“As of [date], cash on hand is $5.2M and quarterly revenue was $670K (≈$2.68M annual run-rate). Current cash supports ~20 months of operations at current burn. We recommend: (1) immediate consolidation of discretionary spend, (2) building a 12–24 month rolling cash forecast with monthly scenarios, and (3) initiating fundraising or strategic options within the next 6–9 months to secure optionality.”

