- Metro Manufacturing has $5.2M in cash and an implied runway of ~20 months, corresponding to an implied net cash burn of $260K/month. Last quarter revenue was $670K (~$223K/month), indicating that current spend materially exceeds recurring revenue.
What this means
- Runway ~20 months is sufficient near-term but requires active cash planning: hiring freezes, discretionary spend review, and contingency plans should be prepared.
- If we do not materially increase revenue or reduce spend, we will need to raise capital or restructure costs within the next 12–18 months to preserve optionality.
