- Revenue covers a portion of monthly outflows; the gap suggests either elevated investment (scaling, inventory, capex) or one-off items.
- The 20-month runway likely assumes current planned investments continue; altering those investments changes runway proportionally.
Risks & caveats
- Revenue volatility, delayed customer payments, or unplanned one-time costs could shorten runway below 20 months.
- Fundraising windows and market conditions may affect ability to raise capital when needed.
Suggested leadership message (short)
- “We currently have $5.2M in cash and a runway of ~20 months at our present plan. To maintain strategic optionality we propose a cost/priority review and preparation of a fundraising or operational contingency plan to be decision-ready within the next 6 months.”
